<body>
<h1>US Tax Calendar — Solopreneur / LLC Reference</h1>
<h2>Federal Deadlines</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Action</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>January 15</td><td>Q4 estimated tax payment</td><td>Prior year Q4 (Sep–Dec)</td></tr><tr><td>January 31</td><td>1099-NEC due to contractors</td><td>Also W-2s if you have employees</td></tr><tr><td>March 15</td><td>S-Corp / Partnership return (Form 1120-S / 1065)</td><td>Or extension Form 7004</td></tr><tr><td>April 15</td><td>Individual / LLC return (Form 1040 + Sch C)</td><td>Also Q1 estimated payment</td></tr><tr><td>April 15</td><td>FBAR due (FinCEN 114)</td><td>If foreign financial accounts &gt; $10K</td></tr><tr><td>April 15</td><td>HSA contribution deadline</td><td>For prior year</td></tr><tr><td>June 15</td><td>Q2 estimated tax payment</td><td>Covers Apr–May income</td></tr><tr><td>September 15</td><td>Q3 estimated tax payment</td><td>Covers Jun–Aug income</td></tr><tr><td>September 15</td><td>S-Corp / Partnership extended return due</td><td>If extension was filed March 15</td></tr><tr><td>October 15</td><td>Individual extended return due</td><td>If extension was filed April 15</td></tr><tr><td>December 31</td><td>Solo 401(k) contribution deadline</td><td>Employee deferral portion</td></tr><tr><td>January 15 (next year)</td><td>Q4 estimated tax payment</td><td>Covers Sep–Dec income</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Year-End Action Deadlines</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Deadline</th><th>Impact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Retirement contributions (Solo 401(k) employee)</td><td>December 31</td><td>Reduces current-year taxable income</td></tr><tr><td>Retirement contributions (SEP-IRA)</td><td>April 15 (or extension)</td><td>Reduces prior-year taxable income</td></tr><tr><td>Section 179 equipment purchases</td><td>December 31</td><td>Full deduction in current year</td></tr><tr><td>Accelerate deductible expenses</td><td>December 31</td><td>Pay before year-end to deduct this year</td></tr><tr><td>Defer income</td><td>December 31</td><td>Invoice late December → collect January</td></tr><tr><td>S-Corp election (Form 2553)</td><td>March 15 for current year</td><td>Must file by 2 months 15 days after tax year start</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Quarterly Payment Schedule (Quick Reference)</h2>
<pre><code>Q1 (Jan–Mar income) → Pay by April 15
Q2 (Apr–May income) → Pay by June 15
Q3 (Jun–Aug income) → Pay by September 15
Q4 (Sep–Dec income) → Pay by January 15 of next year</code></pre>
<p>Note: April 15 covers BOTH the prior-year tax return AND the Q1 estimated payment. These are separate obligations with separate forms (1040 for return, 1040-ES for estimate).</p>
<h2>Penalty Quick Reference</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Penalty</th><th>Rate</th><th>Trigger</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Underpayment (est. tax)</td><td>Federal short-term rate + 3%</td><td>Owe &gt; $1K at filing without safe-harbor coverage</td></tr><tr><td>Late filing</td><td>5% per month (max 25%)</td><td>Return not filed by deadline</td></tr><tr><td>Late payment</td><td>0.5% per month</td><td>Tax not paid by deadline</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy</td><td>20% of underpayment</td><td>Substantial understatement or negligence</td></tr></tbody></table>
